    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (74.62) and **Mickey Moniak** (72.73) anchoring the outfield as our clear-cut elite plays. **Corbin Carroll** thrives in this matchup against Trevor McDonald due to an aggressive green-light environment; the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts the theft probability for our speed-first strategy. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup, making him a high-floor start despite Max Meyer\u2019s competence. **Brice Turang** also surges into the strong-start tier (67.33) as he looks to exploit Andrew Abbott, with the projection model heavily favoring **Brice Turang**\u2019s ability to maximize efficiency against a softer SP_xERA of 4.92.\n\nWhile we remain confident in our starters, the decision to bench **Kyle Karros** (44.41) was razor-thin. **Kyle Karros** posted a respectable projection, but his spot in the bottom third of the lineup\u2014combined with a restrictive 50% hold rate from opposing catchers\u2014ultimately pushed him behind **Zach McKinstry** in the final optimization. We are also keeping a close eye on **James Wood** (66.37); while he ranks as one of our strongest options due to an elite 0.416 xwOBA and favorable wind conditions, he carries a 30% rain risk warning in his matchup against Tolle that could lead to a shortened outing or mid-game postponement. We will monitor the weather closely, ensuring **James Wood** remains in the slot unless conditions deteriorate significantly, which would trigger a move to our bench depth.",
